Problem: Reverse String (LC 344)

Pattern: Two Pointers

Approach:

1. Initialize one pointer at the beginning and another at the end.
2. Swap the characters at both pointers.
3. Move the left pointer toward the right.
4. Move the right pointer toward the left.
5. Continue until both pointers meet or cross.
6. The string is reversed in place, so no extra array is needed.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
